{% extends "quarterly_deep_dive/llm_prompts/base_prompt.j2" %}

{# Specific context for the 'rce_proportion_monthly' chart insight #}
{% set output_format_description = "a concise text block (2-3 sentences) interpreting the trend in the proportion of RCE vulnerabilities" %}

{% block task_instructions %}
Analyze the chart image and data provided below for the chart titled '{{ data_context_payload.chart_caption | default('RCE Proportion Monthly') }}'. This data shows the percentage of total monthly CVEs that were classified as Remote Code Execution (RCE).
Identify the primary trend or the most significant observation regarding the prevalence of RCEs over the period. For example, did the proportion of RCEs increase, decrease, or remain stable? Were there any months with a particularly high or low percentage of RCEs?
Describe this key finding clearly in 2-3 sentences.
{% endblock task_instructions %}

{% block data_context %}
Chart ID: {{ data_context_payload.chart_id | default('rce_proportion_monthly') }}
Chart Caption: {{ data_context_payload.chart_caption | default('Figure 4. Proportion of RCE Vulnerabilities Published Monthly.') }}

Data Summary (Monthly Proportion of RCE CVEs):
{{ data_context_payload.chart_data_summary | default("Data not available.") }}
{% endblock data_context %}
